From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:04:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov5693: Limit the analogue gain to the range the
 sensor follows

The analogue gain control ranges from 1 to 2047 in sixteenths. On a
Surface Pro 9 the sensor follows the register from 16 (1x) to 992 (62x):
the mean of a raw frame doubles with the value over that range. From 993
on the image drops back to what 512 (32x) gives and stays there up to
1023, and 1024 to 2047 repeat lower gains. Values below 16 attenuate,
which keeps saturated pixels below white.

An auto exposure loop that is told the gain reaches 127.9x raises it
past 62x in dim light and gets a darker image for it, so it raises it
further; libcamera's software ISP ends up at the maximum with a quarter
of the brightness it could have, and oscillates on the way.

Make the range 16 to 992.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
index 47a72895b..4f793476c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
@@ -54,8 +54,13 @@
 /* Analogue Gain */
 #define OV5693_GAIN_CTRL_REG			CCI_REG16(0x350a)
 #define OV5693_GAIN_CTRL_MASK			GENMASK(10, 0)
-#define OV5693_GAIN_MIN				1
-#define OV5693_GAIN_MAX				2047
+/*
+ * Sixteenths. The sensor follows the value from 1x (16) to 62x (992); below
+ * 16 it attenuates, and from 993 on the gain falls back to 32x and stops
+ * following the value.
+ */
+#define OV5693_GAIN_MIN				16
+#define OV5693_GAIN_MAX				992
 #define OV5693_GAIN_DEF				16
 #define OV5693_GAIN_STEP			1
 
